>North Bank</h4><dl><div><dt>Depth</dt><dd>34 → 48 cm</dd></div><div><dt>Salt</dt><dd>34 → 36 ppt</dd></div><div><dt>Oxygen</dt><dd>64 → 67 %</dd></div><div><dt>Life</dt><dd>44 → 48 %</dd></div><div><dt>Canopy</dt><dd>0 → 1 / 3</dd></div></dl></section><section class=\"journal-cell\" data-cell-id=\"heart\"><h4>Heart Pool</h4><dl><div><dt>Depth</dt><dd>56 → 70 cm</dd></div><div><dt>Salt</dt><dd>30 → 34 ppt</dd></div><div><dt>Oxygen</dt><dd>55 → 54 %</dd></div><div><dt>Life</dt><dd>49 → 50 %</dd></div><div><dt>Canopy</dt><dd>0 → 0 / 3</dd></div></dl></section><section class=\"journal-cell\" data-cell-id=\"south\"><h4>South Reach</h4><dl><div><dt>Depth</dt><dd>67 → 81 cm</dd></div><div><dt>Salt</dt><dd>40 → 43 ppt</dd></div><div><dt>Oxygen</dt><dd>43 → 40 %</dd></div><div><dt>Life</dt><dd>38 → 38 %</dd></div><div><dt>Canopy</dt><dd>0 → 0 / 3</dd></div></dl></section></div></div></details></li><li data-tide=\"2\"><details class=\"journal-tide\"><summary><span class=\"journal-choice\">Tide 2 · Shade · North Bank</span><span class=\"journal-event\">Neap ebb</span></summary><div class=\"journal-tide-body\"><p class=\"journal-event-note\">A short, quiet ebb leaves pools exposed.</p><h3>Full field notes</h3><ul class=\"journal-notes\"><li>Reed-bed shade · North Bank: canopy 1→2, salt 36→34 ppt, oxygen 67→71%, biomass 48→51%. Canopy blunts heat and drying.</li><li>Neap ebb · all three cells: water -5 cm, salt +2 ppt; North Bank oxygen 71→74%. A short, quiet ebb leaves pools exposed.</li><li>Dawn drift · suitable depth/salt/oxygen → biomass +2, dawn oxygen +2; the water-depth/salinity rule shifts salt 0 ppt.</li><li>Net · North Bank: water 48→43 cm, salt 36→36 ppt, oxygen 67→76%, biomass 48→53%.</li></ul><h3>Before → after this tide</h3><p class=\"journal-resources\">Freshwater: 5 → 5. Seed packs: 5 → 5.</p><div class=\"journal-cells\"><section class=\"journal-cell\" data-cell-id=\"north\"><h4>North Bank</h4><dl><div><dt>Depth</dt><dd>48 → 43 cm</dd></div><div><dt>Salt</dt><dd>36 → 36 ppt</dd></div><div><dt>Oxygen</dt><dd>67 → 76 %</dd></div><div><dt>Life</dt><dd>48 → 53 %</dd></div><div><dt>Canopy</dt><dd>1 → 2 / 3</dd></div></dl></section><section class=\"journal-cell\" data-cell-id=\"heart\"><h4>Heart Pool</h4><dl><div><dt>Depth</dt><dd>70 → 65 cm</dd></div><div><dt>Salt</dt><dd>34 → 36 ppt</dd></div><div><dt>Oxygen</dt><dd>54 → 59 %</dd></div><div><dt>Life</dt><dd>50 → 51 %</dd></div><div><dt>Canopy</dt><dd>0 → 0 / 3</dd></div></dl></section><section class=\"journal-cell\" data-cell-id=\"south\"><h4>South Reach</h4><dl><div><dt>Depth</dt><dd>81 → 76 cm</dd></div><div><dt>Salt</dt><dd>43 → 45 ppt</dd></div><div><dt>Oxygen</dt><dd>40 → 43 %</dd></div><div><dt>Life</dt><dd>38 → 38 %</dd></div><div><dt>Canopy</dt><dd>0 → 0 / 3</dd></div></dl></section></div></div></details></li><li data-tide=\"3\"><details class=\"journal-tide\"><summary><span class=\"journal-choice\">Tide 3 · Shade · North Bank</span><span class=\"journal-event\">Heat pulse</span></summary><div class=\"journal-tide-body\"><p class=\"journal-event-note\">Hot air accelerates evaporation and oxygen loss.</p><h3>Full field notes</h3><ul class=\"journal-notes\"><li>Reed-bed shade · North Bank: canopy 2→3, salt 36→34 ppt, oxygen 76→80%, biomass 53→56%. Canopy blunts heat and drying.</li><li>Heat pulse · all three cells: water -8 cm, salt +7 ppt; North Bank oxygen 80→79% (canopy relief +6). Hot air accelerates evaporation and oxygen loss.</li><li>Dawn drift · suitable depth/salt/oxygen → biomass +2, dawn oxygen +2; the water-depth/salinity rule shifts salt 0 ppt.</li><li>Net · North Bank: water 43→35 cm, salt 36→41 ppt, oxygen 76→81%, biomass 53→58%.</li></ul><h3>Before → after this tide</h3><p class=\"journal-resources\">Freshwater: 5 → 5. Seed packs: 5 → 5.</p><div class=\"journal-cells\"><section class=\"journal-cell\" data-cell-id=\"north\"><h4>North Bank</h4><dl><div><dt>Depth</dt><dd>43 → 35 cm</dd></div><div><dt>Salt</dt><dd>36 → 41 ppt</dd></div><div><dt>Oxygen</dt><dd>76 → 81 %</dd></div><div><dt>Life</dt><dd>53 → 58 %</dd></div><div><dt>Canopy</dt><dd>2 → 3 / 3</dd></div></dl></section><section class=\"journal-cell\" data-cell-id=\"heart\"><h4>Heart Pool</h4><dl><div><dt>Depth</dt><dd>65 → 57 cm</dd></div><div><dt>Salt</dt><dd>36 → 43 ppt</dd></div><div><dt>Oxygen</dt><dd>59 → 54 %</dd></div><div><dt>Life</dt><dd>51 → 50 %</dd></div><div><dt>Canopy</dt><dd>0 → 0 / 3</dd></div></dl></section><section class=\"journal-cell\" data-cell-id=\"south\"><h4>South Reach</h4><dl><div><dt>Depth</dt><dd>76 → 68 cm</dd></div><div><dt>Salt</dt><dd>45 → 52 ppt</dd></div><div><dt>Oxygen</dt><dd>43 → 38 %</dd></div><div><dt>Life</dt><dd>38 → 37 %</dd></div><div><dt>Canopy</dt><dd>0 → 0 / 3</dd></div></dl></section></div></div></details></li><li data-tide=\"4\"><details class=\"journal-tide\"><summary><span class=\"journal-choice\">Tide 4 · Shade · Heart Pool</span><span class=\"journal-event\">Runoff plume</span></summary><div class=\"journal-tide-body\"><p class=\"journal-event-note\">Fresh upland runoff dilutes the channel edge.</p><h3>Full field notes</h3><ul class=\"journal-notes\"><li>Reed-bed shade · Heart Pool: canopy 0→1, salt 43→41 ppt, oxygen 54→58%, biomass 50→53%. Canopy blunts heat and drying.</li><li>Runoff plume · all three cells: water +9 cm, salt -11 ppt; Heart Pool oxygen 58→60%. Fresh upland runoff dilutes the channel edge.</li><li>Dawn drift · suitable depth/salt/oxygen → biomass +1, dawn oxygen +2; the water-depth/salinity rule shifts salt 0 ppt.</li><li>Net · Heart Pool: water 57→66 cm, salt 43→30 ppt, oxygen 54→62%, biomass 50→54%.</li></ul><h3>Before → after this tide</h3><p class=\"journal-resources\">Freshwater: 5 → 5. Seed packs: 5 → 5.</p><div class=\"journal-cells\"><section class=\"journal-cell\" data-cell-id=\"north\"><h4>North Bank</h4><dl><div><dt>Depth</dt><dd>35 → 44 cm</dd></div><div><dt>Salt</dt><dd>41 → 30 ppt</dd></div><div><dt>Oxygen</dt><dd>81 → 85 %</dd></div><div><dt>Life</dt><dd>58 → 60 %</dd></div><di